## Feature user guides (`docs/features/`)

**User-facing docs** — what the app does and how to use it. Not progress trackers (those stay in RFC/issue).

Index: [features/README.md](../../docs/features/README.md) · Template: [TEMPLATE.md](../../docs/features/TEMPLATE.md)

### When to update (mandatory — same turn as code)

Update the matching feature doc **whenever user-visible behavior changes** — not only when an RFC ships.

| Code change | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Nav tab added/removed/renamed, shell chrome, default tabs | [getting-started/navigation.md](../../docs/features/getting-started/navigation.md) · [settings/navigation-bar.md](../../docs/features/settings/navigation-bar.md) |
| Settings screen: new toggle, moved section, renamed label | Matching `docs/features/settings/*.md` |
| Player controls, PiP, subtitles, speed, next episode | Matching `docs/features/playback/*.md` |
| Scraper/source/provider behavior users configure or see | `docs/features/scrapers/*` · `docs/features/sources/*` |
| Tab feature UX (`apps/forja/lib/features/<name>/`) | Matching `docs/features/**/<name>.md` (or add one) |
| Platform limits (torrent hidden, constrained profile) | Affected feature doc + [platforms.md](../../docs/features/getting-started/platforms.md) if cross-cutting |
| Feature ships (was stub / coming soon) | Move doc out of `coming-soon/`; add to [features README](../../docs/features/README.md) |
| Feature removed or permanently disabled | Update doc honestly or move to coming-soon with “removed” note — do not describe dead UI |

### What to keep accurate

Each feature file ([TEMPLATE.md](../../docs/features/TEMPLATE.md)) must reflect **current** app behavior:

- **How to open it** — nav path, settings path, entry points (must match live UI)
- **What you can do** — actions the user can actually perform today
- **Setup** — keys, OAuth, URLs the settings screen still uses
- **Tips / Related** — cross-links still valid

**Read the code or run the UI before editing.** Do not copy from RFCs or stale docs — code is source of truth ([honesty-and-completion.mdc](./honesty-and-completion.mdc)).

### New or renamed features

1. Create or rename `docs/features/<category>/<slug>.md` from [TEMPLATE.md](../../docs/features/TEMPLATE.md)
2. Add link in [features/README.md](../../docs/features/README.md) (and **I want to…** table if user-facing)
3. Grep `docs/features/` for old slug/path and fix cross-links

RFC/issue track **implementation status**; feature docs track **how it works for users**. Both update in the same turn when behavior changes.

---

## RFC ↔ issue

| Layer | Owns | When status changes |
|-------|------|---------------------|
| **RFC** `003-[partial]-….md` | Feature spec + full acceptance | **Same file** — status changes only when implementation state changes |
| **Issue** `018-[open]-….md` | Bug, debt, verifiable sub-work | **Same file** — `[fixed]` or `[canceled]` when done or abandoned |

Ship version is **changelog + git tag**, not RFC/issue filenames or bodies.

### Scope big work before coding

When the user asks for something **substantial** — **create or extend docs first**, then implement. Do not jump straight to code without a tracked spec.

**Substantial = needs an RFC or issue:**

| Kind | Create | Examples |
|------|--------|----------|
| **RFC** | New `docs/rfc/NNN-[draft\|planned\|open\|partial]-….md` | New feature subsystem, multi-component architectural change, new acceptance slice that does not fit an existing RFC |
| **Issue** | New `docs/issues/NNN-[draft\|open]-….md` | Concrete bug, engine debt, test gap, verifiable sub-work with its own fix |
| **Extend existing** | Add rows to **existing** RFC/issue tables | Fits current RFC-023 scope → add `R23-A*` rows; do **not** clone a new RFC number |

**Same turn — mandatory checklist when creating:**

1. **Pick next free number** — grep `docs/rfc/` and `docs/issues/` for highest NNN; use NNN+1
2. **Create the file** — full mandatory format ([Progress tracker](#progress-tracker-format-mandatory--rfc--issue--migration), glance, legend, emoji task tables). New RFCs start `[draft]` or `[planned]`; new issues `[draft]` until work starts → `[open]`
3. **Update indexes** — [RFC README](../../docs/rfc/README.md) and/or [issues README](../../docs/issues/README.md) **Progress** column
4. Do **not** add `**Target version:**` or backlog links to the RFC/issue body

**If the ask is small** (one file, obvious fix inside an existing RFC slice): extend that RFC’s task table — no new RFC/issue file.

**Do not wait** for the user to say “create the RFC” — if the work is big and untracked, file the RFC/issue in the **same turn** as you start (or before) implementation.

### Partial RFC — do not split

Ship incrementally from **one RFC per feature**. Use slices inside the spec, not new RFC numbers.

**Inside the RFC:**

- `## Components` + `## Acceptance (slice)` emoji task tables — flip row Status when code ships
- Optional `## Slices` prose mapping ID ranges to work batches

**RFC status:**

- Stays `[partial]` until **all** acceptance rows ✅ for that RFC → then `[fixed]`
- Do **not** rename to `[fixed]` because one slice shipped

### When to split vs nest

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Same feature, shipped in chunks | **One RFC** — slices/phases inside |
| Different subsystem, independent ship/cancel | **Separate RFCs** (e.g. sync vs watch party) |
| Release theme / milestone index | **Meta RFC** (e.g. v1.2 bundle) — links to child RFCs; spec stays in each child |
| Concrete bug, test gap, debt with own fix | **Child issue** (parent links 019–022 pattern) |

**Do not** invent IDs outside the prefixes in [Progress tracker format](#progress-tracker-format-mandatory--rfc--issue--migration). Migration `P2-XX` IDs stay in migration docs only.

**Do not:** clone an RFC for the next version; put semver in RFC filenames; use `[canceled]` when you mean deferred.

---

## On status change

1. Rename file (tag + move to terminal folder when `fixed` / `canceled`)
2. Update `**Status:**` in body
3. Update the folder README index
4. Grep old path in `docs/` and fix links

## After code changes (mandatory — same turn)

When you land or materially advance work tied to an RFC, issue, or **user-visible feature**, **do not stop at code**. Update docs in the **same turn**:

1. **RFC** — flip `R*-C*` / `R*-A*` rows; update glance **Progress** / **Current slice**; `**Status:**` if terminal
2. **Issue** — flip `I*-A*` / `I*-T*` rows; update glance **Progress**; filename tag if terminal
3. **Feature user guide** — update matching `docs/features/**/*.md` so How to open / What you can do / Setup match the code you just changed (see [Feature user guides](#feature-user-guides-docsfeatures))
4. **Changelog** — add, edit, or remove bullets in the active `docs/changelog/*-[draft].md`; final truth only (see [changelog](../../.cursor/rules/changelog.mdc))
5. **Indexes** — RFC README **Progress**; issues README **Progress**; features README when adding/removing pages
6. **Cross-links** — grep old filename slug under `docs/` and fix

**Forbidden:** code shipped with task rows still ⬜; aggregate-only glance with no item table; checkbox lists parallel to emoji tables; feature docs describing UI that no longer exists.

Skip RFC/issue updates only when the change is unrelated to any RFC (pure refactor, typo, tooling). **Still update feature docs and changelog** if user-visible behavior changed. **Never** update `docs/backlog/` as part of this checklist.

| Folder | Terminal folders | Terminal statuses |
|--------|------------------|-------------------|
| `rfc/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |
| `issues/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |
| `migration/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |

## Migration (`docs/migration/`)

Engine migration phases — numbered `01`–`03`, not RFCs. Same [Progress tracker format](#progress-tracker-format-mandatory--rfc--issue--migration).

### Filename tags

`[draft]` · `[open]` · `[partial]` · `[fixed]` (in `fixed/`) · `[canceled]` (in `canceled/`)

Pattern: `NN-[{status}]-slug.md` — e.g. `01-[fixed]-rust-engine.md`

| Body status | Filename | Location |
|-------------|----------|----------|
| `draft` | `NN-[draft]-….md` | Phase scoped, not started |
| `open` | `NN-[open]-….md` | Actively migrating |
| `partial` | `NN-[partial]-….md` | In progress |
| `fixed` | `NN-[fixed]-….md` | `docs/migration/fixed/` |
| `canceled` | `NN-[canceled]-….md` | `docs/migration/canceled/` |

All current phases (1–3) are **`fixed`** in `fixed/`. Index: [migration/README.md](../../docs/migration/README.md).
